WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.232
The storm ended just as quickly as it began—almost as if it had never happened. The

2
00:00:07.233 --> 00:00:11.613
next day was sunny, beautiful, and calm once again. The

3
00:00:11.614 --> 00:00:15.499
boat, however, did not survive the wind and rain. When

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:23.037
Tommy opened his eyes, he found himself still holding onto the mast. There

5
00:00:23.038 --> 00:00:25.753
were pieces of wood everywhere. Tommy

6
00:00:25.754 --> 00:00:28.982
even saw the boat’s wheel floating by. But

7
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:33.814
there were no signs of Dr. Dolittle, Charles, or Polynesia. He

8
00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:37.621
was all alone. "I

9
00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:39.139
will not cry," Tommy

10
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.194
said as he wiped away his tears. "They

11
00:00:42.195 --> 00:00:44.368
are alive, I know it!" Tommy

12
00:00:44.369 --> 00:00:47.377
tried to think of happy thoughts. "Someone

13
00:00:47.378 --> 00:00:49.016
will find me. I

14
00:00:49.017 --> 00:00:53.123
will be together with my friends again," he said aloud. At

15
00:00:53.124 --> 00:00:58.139
that moment, Tommy looked into the water and screamed. There

16
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.667
were two scary sharks swimming around him. "Go

17
00:01:01.668 --> 00:01:04.699
away, please," he whispered. One

18
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.642
shark poked his head out of the water. "He

19
00:01:07.643 --> 00:01:11.352
doesn’t look too good," he said to his friend. The

20
00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:14.743
other came out of the water and looked at Tommy. "Not

21
00:01:14.744 --> 00:01:19.433
much meat on him, is there?" "Did

22
00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:21.724
you find anything else around? Something

23
00:01:21.725 --> 00:01:25.617
tastier?" the first shark licked its lips. "Nope.

24
00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:32.274
This small human is the only thing I can see," the second one said. Tommy

25
00:01:32.275 --> 00:01:35.190
wished he could speak their language. He

26
00:01:35.191 --> 00:01:38.542
decided to use what he had already learned. "Oink,

27
00:01:38.543 --> 00:01:46.101
quack, hee-haw, woof-woof," he said. The

28
00:01:46.102 --> 00:01:48.207
sharks looked confused. "What’s

29
00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.692
he doing?" one asked. "Don’t

30
00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:53.415
ask me," said the other. "I

31
00:01:53.416 --> 00:01:56.603
can never understand these humans." "Shall

32
00:01:56.604 --> 00:01:58.767
we eat him or not?" But

33
00:01:58.768 --> 00:02:06.274
before they could decide, a long, horrible screeching sound was heard. Tommy

34
00:02:06.275 --> 00:02:08.735
and the sharks looked up. "Polynesia!"

35
00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:12.134
cried Tommy joyfully. She

36
00:02:12.135 --> 00:02:16.134
swooped down and started to bite the sharks’ noses. "Shame

37
00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.342
on you! Trying

38
00:02:17.343 --> 00:02:21.196
to eat a helpless boy!" she scolded them. "That

39
00:02:21.197 --> 00:02:29.540
hurts!" "Aw!" the sharks cried and dived back into the water.

40
00:02:29.541 --> 00:02:32.576
Tommy was so happy to see his friend.

41
00:02:32.577 --> 00:02:34.833
He could not stop crying.

42
00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:39.238
"Now, now, Tommy," said the parrot, comforting him.

43
00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:43.741
"What about the doctor? Charles?" Tommy sobbed.

44
00:02:43.742 --> 00:02:45.950
"We’re all safe."

45
00:02:45.951 --> 00:02:49.390
Polynesia explained everything that had happened.

46
00:02:49.391 --> 00:02:52.988
The doctor and Charles are on land, waiting for you.

47
00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:56.097
So we should go to them as soon as possible."

48
00:02:56.098 --> 00:02:58.296
"But how?" asked Tommy.

49
00:02:58.297 --> 00:03:00.831
"I don’t have anything to row with."

50
00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:03.684
"We don’t need oars," she replied.

51
00:03:03.685 --> 00:03:06.205
"Our friends will help us."

52
00:03:06.206 --> 00:03:10.320
Tommy suddenly felt the mast gliding along in the water.

53
00:03:10.321 --> 00:03:14.028
"Hold on tight," Polynesia called out.

54
00:03:14.029 --> 00:03:17.964
Tommy turned around to see two beautiful dolphins.

55
00:03:17.965 --> 00:03:22.033
They were using their long noses to push the mast forward.

56
00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:28.790
Tommy wanted to reach out and touch their smooth, shiny skin.

57
00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:33.273
"Everything okay?" Polynesia called out to the dolphins.

58
00:03:33.274 --> 00:03:34.550
"It certainly is!

59
00:03:34.551 --> 00:03:37.563
He’s light as a feather!" one replied.

60
00:03:37.564 --> 00:03:42.838
"Not like Dr. Dolittle and that other man," called out the other.

61
00:03:42.839 --> 00:03:46.401
"Now that was heavy!"

62
00:03:46.402 --> 00:03:51.033
The dolphins laughed out cheerfully.

63
00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:55.588
"Yes, Dr. Dolittle told me he’d put on some weight," laughed Tommy.

64
00:03:55.589 --> 00:03:57.716
Polynesia stared at Tommy.

65
00:03:57.717 --> 00:04:02.112
The dolphins stopped pushing and poked their heads out of the water.

66
00:04:02.113 --> 00:04:05.456
Tommy did not know why everyone was looking at him.

67
00:04:05.457 --> 00:04:10.383
"Did I say something wrong?" he asked shyly.

68
00:04:10.384 --> 00:04:13.212
"Tommy," Polynesia said finally,

69
00:04:13.213 --> 00:04:17.068
"just now, you understood our language and spoke it."

70
00:04:17.069 --> 00:04:20.745
"What?" Tommy shook his head in confusion.

71
00:04:20.746 --> 00:04:23.486
He thought about what had just happened.

72
00:04:23.487 --> 00:04:27.731
Yes, he clearly understood what the dolphins said.

73
00:04:27.732 --> 00:04:30.303
"Oh, my!" he exclaimed.

74
00:04:30.304 --> 00:04:35.355
"I can speak! I can speak!"

75
00:04:35.356 --> 00:04:38.213
Soon, Tommy saw the island ahead.

76
00:04:38.214 --> 00:04:42.384
Dr. Dolittle and Charles were waving their hands excitedly.

77
00:04:42.385 --> 00:04:45.104
Tommy did not know what made him happier:

78
00:04:45.105 --> 00:04:50.430
seeing his friends again or finally being able to speak animal language.

79
00:04:50.431 --> 00:04:57.420
He decided that both things made him equally happy.

